Z||000000||Philphine||03-08-2001||01:10 PM||||<BR>fooled around with this latest fiero a bit. finally tried getting the engine compartment lid off. first thing i noticed is it has headers on it. those might get transfered to the indy. i noticed though that each pipe has a dent in it right as it comes from the head like someone hit each pipe with a hammer. can't imagine that would help flow much. i'm wondering if it could be rpaired or if it's worth worrying about. i'm wondering what other mods i should look out for when i have more time (better intake, throttle body, etc.) <P>also the oil dipstick is on the firewall side of the engne. maybe it's from a front wheel drive car?<P><P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe (cheap thrill)<BR>'84 chop top (parts car or project. time will tell)||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||03-08-2001||01:23 PM||||if it's anything like the headers we had on the saturn or the ones on the Miata.. those "dents" are there for access to the manifold bolts. but yeah you can fix em.. use an exhaust pipe expander (about $10 at NAPA)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||03-08-2001||02:56 PM||||hmm... don't know enough about headers to have come to that conclusion. guess i should try getting to the bolts to see if thats what they're for before i try anything. thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||03-09-2001||09:25 AM||||i try not to put things back to the top just for having them up there but i was hoing someone might know why the dipstick is on the firewall side of the engine.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wolfhound||03-09-2001||09:39 AM||||Philphine, Isn't that where it is supposed to be? 4 cylinder right!||||reg||5
Z||000005||Rodrv6||03-09-2001||11:00 AM||||The original location for the dipstick on the 84 Dukes is up front by the firewall.  They were moved to the end of the cylinder head above the transaxle during one of the recalls.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||4
Z||000006||Philphine||03-09-2001||11:07 AM||||thanks rod. hmm...one more thing to wonder about with this car. maybe it got customised all the way back in '84 and no recall work was done. <P>1st time i've seen a dipstick like this wolfhound. i have 3 other fieros, 2 are '84's and they all have the dipstick on the trunk side of the engine compartment.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Tigger||03-09-2001||11:21 AM||||The oil dipstick is on the firewall side on my '84 SE like yours.  A previous owner replaced the ol'duke with a new Goodwrench crate motor long ago so I don't know if this is the original location.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 03-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Wolfhound||03-09-2001||12:16 PM||||Philphine, I have 2 84s,a 85,86,87,and an 88 that all have the dipstick to the firewall side of the thermostat. The tube goes to the firewall side of the engine.<BR> I think I see what you're saying from Rodv6,s post, that it,s some where midway of the engine and behind it? I haven't seen that.||||reg||1
